    },
    {
      "applies_to_keys": ["odd_product", "outcome_traversal"],
      "conditions": ["The profile treats edge traversal as the unit of compute."],
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 634,
          "quote": "Because this profile makes an edge traversal the unit of compute, an ODD\nproduct must use that unit of compute to build its own operative framework\nbehaviour. The required order is: declare the outcome\ntraversal over typed assets; publish the declarative GTL/ABG carrier\nstructure; implement only the minimal imperative adapter code that remains\nnecessary (P0, P6).",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F11.%20Core%20law%2F11.2A%20Outcome-first%20realisation%20order",
          "start_line": 629
        },
        {
          "end_line": 652,
          "quote": "Imperative code must not own domain meaning,\nsemantic target movement, step selection, closure semantics, lineage truth\nor constructive workflow truth. Framework behaviour implemented\nimperatively first and only later described in GTL vocabulary is\nODD-shaped but not yet ODD-built (P6, P0).",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F11.%20Core%20law%2F11.2A%20Outcome-first%20realisation%20order",
          "start_line": 648
