      "statement": "The live line must publish a machine-readable function catalogue; at minimum each retained function should expose name, inputs, outputs, intent and public/helper role. A prose-only or prompt-memory-only callable surface leaves the product under-built. The product must publish public carriers, their graphs, typed node/vector surfaces and bound semantic jobs or equivalent outer callable contracts. Callers never bind directly to hidden inner vectors. Where public carriers refine, live traversal boundaries are explicitly published through lawful surfaces such as RefinementBoundary or CandidateFamily, while the outer carrier stays the callable contract.",
